    Headline
        query the geometry, operations and numerical classes of a realized variety
    Description
        Text
            Every supported model reports its dimension, geometric evidence, Serre shift,
            distinguished objects and operation scope. Numerical classes belong to one
            model. The Euler pairing on K3 surfaces is the negative Mukai pairing. The
            quintic uses an alternating Euler form.
///

doc ///
    Key
        QuinticThreefold
        quinticThreefold
        QuinticNumericalClass
        quinticClass
        (quinticClass, QuinticThreefold, List)
        QuinticObjectReference
        ShiftedQuinticObject
        SymbolicQuinticTwistImage
        (catalogueObject, QuinticThreefold, String)
        (structureObject, QuinticThreefold)
        (sphericalObject, QuinticObjectReference)
        (pointSheaf, QuinticThreefold)
        (pointIdealSheaf, QuinticThreefold)
        (shiftObject, QuinticObjectReference, ZZ)
        (shiftObject, ShiftedQuinticObject, ZZ)
        (applyWord, SphericalTwistWord, QuinticObjectReference)
        (applyWordToClass, SphericalTwistWord, QuinticNumericalClass)
        (realizeTwistImage, QuinticObjectReference)
        (cohomologyObservation, QuinticObjectReference)
        (extObservation, QuinticObjectReference, QuinticObjectReference)
    Headline
        work with the marked Fermat quintic threefold
    Description
        Text
            The model is the smooth Fermat quintic over ZZ/101 with the marked point
            (1:-1:0:0:0). The Jacobian checks smoothness. Adjunction gives the trivial
            canonical bundle and Serre shift 3. The numerical class uses only the subgroup
            generated by the structure sheaf and the marked point sheaf. Their Euler
            pairings in the two orders are 1 and -1, by projective cohomology and Serre duality.
            The signed action is the Euler transvection in this subgroup.
        Text
            The explicit strategy supports the forward structure twist of the marked point.
            The cone of the surjection to the point represents its ideal sheaf shifted by one.
            Other word patterns can be inspected symbolically and return capability evidence
            when requested for realization.
        Example
            Y = quinticThreefold();
            Oref = structureObject Y;
            P = catalogueObject(Y,"O_x");
            (varietyDimension Y, serreShift Y)
            cohomologyObservation Oref
            extObservation(P,Oref)
            W = twistWord {twistStep(sphericalObject Oref,1)};
            A = realizeTwistImage applyWord(W,P);
            numericalClass A
            A
///
